From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Helen Kwok <107752876+helenkwok@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:19:16 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] fix(arch): set IP_MULTICAST_IF with an in_addr on non-Linux
 POSIX

Only Linux takes the struct ip_mreqn that setupMulticastRequest builds there.
Elsewhere the request is a struct ip_mreq, and IP_MULTICAST_IF takes just the
interface address, as the Apple branch already passed it.

On QNX 8.0 the 8-byte struct ip_mreq is rejected with EADDRNOTAVAIL, so
every IPv4 multicast PubSub connection fails to open. With this change the
PubSub unit tests that use 224.0.0.22 pass on QNX 8.0 (aarch64le).
---
 arch/posix/eventloop_posix_udp.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/posix/eventloop_posix_udp.c b/arch/posix/eventloop_posix_udp.c
index ab1de8f8..d417b640 100644
--- a/arch/posix/eventloop_posix_udp.c
+++ b/arch/posix/eventloop_posix_udp.c
@@ -489,7 +489,9 @@ setupSendMultiCast(UA_FD fd, struct addrinfo *info, const UA_KeyValueMap *params
     UA_RESET_ERRNO;
     int result = -1;
     if(info->ai_family == AF_INET && multiCastType == MULTICASTTYPE_IPV4) {
-#if defined(__APPLE__)
+        /* Linux takes the struct ip_mreqn. Elsewhere the request is a struct
+         * ip_mreq, but IP_MULTICAST_IF takes only the interface address. */
+#if !defined(__linux__)
         result = UA_setsockopt(fd, IPPROTO_IP, IP_MULTICAST_IF,
                             &req.ipv4.imr_interface, sizeof(struct in_addr));
 #else
